# A Luxel library scene — Apache-2.0. Grammar: library/README.md "Strips".
# layout: strip
# Two zones on one strip, WLED-segment style: fire on the first 75 px, the sea
# on the rest, and a warm glow breathing where they meet. A pattern layer is a
# WINDOW onto that pattern's own full-strip render, so the fire (rooted at
# pixel 0, burning toward the seam) is its own pixels 0..74. The sea is the
# BASE, the whole strip mirrored (`flipx`, flags 3): its far end meets the
# fire, and on a 150 px strip pixels 75..149 are its own 74..0 run backwards.
# It is the base rather than a `75 0 0 0` segment because a zero `w` is the
# layout's width, not "what is left": the box overhangs the end, a flip
# mirrors the whole overhanging box, and the visible part comes out black
# (library/README.md "Strips"). The glow is three nested colour boxes in
# `add` — 10, 4 and 2 px wide, each brighter than the last — a soft ramp a
# box can stand in for, the core breathing on a 4 s keyframe track.
# Authored for a 150 px strip. The seam sits at pixel 75 whatever the length
# (a box is in pixels): on 300 px the fire keeps its 75 and the sea gets the
# other 225; under 75 px — a 60 px strip — the seam falls off the end and the
# strip is all fire. For another split, move the fire's 75 and the glow boxes
# (70, 73, 74) together.
S - Fire & Water
L pat 0 0 0 0 normal 100 none fill 3
N Sea
I @pat/ocean
C sliderPalette 65536
C sliderFoamPct 3932160
L pat 0 0 75 0 normal 100 none fill 1
N Fire
I @pat/perlin-fire
L color 70 0 10 0 add 22 none fill 1
N Glow
K ff9a4a
L color 73 0 4 0 add 40 none fill 1
N Glow 2
K ffc880
L color 74 0 2 0 add 60 none fill 1
N Core
K fff2d8
#   ms    x  y  opacity ease
M 0       =  =  35      sine
M 2000    =  =  80      sine
M 4000    =  =  35      sine
